Px test fonts (Px*.ttf, PxIcons-Regular.woff, *.woff2), web-font fixtures
  Source:   generated by crates/px-text/examples/fixture_fonts.rs
            (`cargo run -p px-text --example fixture_fonts -- tests/fonts`); the
            bytes are a pure function of that file. Original work, CC0.
  Content:  six TrueType fonts of straight-edged polygons, a few KB each: Px Text
            (Regular hollow bars, Bold solid bars, Italic slanted), Px Serif, Px
            Mono, and Px Icons (private-use U+E000..U+E004). Letters and digits map
            to bars whose height depends on the character; they are shapes, not
            letterforms. Used by tests/render (webfont-*, font-generics) and by
            crates/px-text/tests/webfont.rs, crates/px-shell/tests/webfonts.rs.
  Wrapped:  PxIcons-Regular.woff, PxIcons-Regular.woff2, PxText-Regular.woff2 and
            PxText-Bold.woff2 were made from the .ttf files with fontTools 4.68
            (`TTFont(src); font.flavor = "woff" | "woff2"; font.save(dst)`, Brotli
            1.2.1) as an independent encoder for the decoders in crates/px-text.
            Regenerating the .ttf files does not require fontTools; regenerating
            the wrapped ones does, and is only needed if the .ttf bytes change.
